cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file and the version-specific Zenodo record."
title: "amr-clonalshare: lineage structure in antimicrobial susceptibility tables, and the lineage share that censored MIC readings guarantee"
abstract: >-
  Lineage shares of antimicrobial phenotypes from exported susceptibility
  tables and a lineage column, without genomes. For MICs, the lineage share
  of the MIC ordering, an analogue of the rank intraclass correlation
  extended to readings censored on laboratory-specific panels, with an
  interval for the lineages in hand and a permutation test within
  laboratories, and bounds on the lineage share of the unobserved MIC
  ordering whose lower end, the share the readings guarantee, is computed
  with a certified error. Also the lineage share of binary calls, a
  decomposition of prevalence differences, a comparison of lineage
  definitions that separates record selection, singletons and relabelling,
  with paired intervals for its terms.
